+# Best AI Tools for Restaurants in 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-restaurants-2026?style=social)
+
+> Best AI tools for restaurants in 2026 are still a niche in open source, so this list focuses on the strongest self-hosted GitHub projects restaurants can actually adapt for phone ordering, menu OCR, staff copilots, demand forecasting, and reservations. Every entry below is a public GitHub repository, and categories with thin restaurant-specific coverage are called out honestly as gaps.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `tastyigniter/TastyIgniter` is the strongest restaurant-specific open source platform in this list for online ordering, reservations, and restaurant operations.
+- `pipecat-ai/pipecat`, `Intervo/Intervo`, and `RasaHQ/rasa` are the most practical foundations for AI phone ordering, reservations, and support agents.
+- `PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR`, `JaidedAI/EasyOCR`, and `tesseract-ocr/tesseract` are the best menu digitization and document OCR picks.
+- `langgenius/dify`, `FlowiseAI/Flowise`, `Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm`, and `open-webui/open-webui` are the easiest ways to ship self-hosted restaurant copilots and knowledge bots.
+- `Nixtla/neuralforecast`, `unit8co/darts`, and `sktime/pytorch-forecasting` are the strongest open source forecasting stacks for demand, staffing, and inventory planning.
+
+## Why This List
+Restaurants need AI tools they can audit, self-host, and integrate with their own menus, POS data, reservation workflows, and support channels. The best AI tools for restaurants in 2026 are not mostly restaurant-only products on GitHub; the real open source opportunity is combining restaurant software with general-purpose voice AI, OCR, RAG, and forecasting projects that restaurants can run without proprietary SaaS lock-in.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Voice, Chat, and Phone Ordering Agents
+
+#### [Pipecat](https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat)
+> **Description:** Pipecat is an open source Python framework for real-time voice and multimodal conversational agents. Its README focuses on streaming voice assistants, business agents, composable pipelines, and integrations for speech recognition, text-to-speech, and transport layers. For restaurants, that maps well to phone ordering, reservation intake, FAQ automation, and kiosk-style assistants. GitHub shows strong recent activity and a permissive BSD license, which makes it attractive as a customizable voice layer rather than a fixed app. Last commit: Mar 30, 2026. Stars: 10,940. Primary language: Python. License: BSD-2-Clause.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat](https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat)
+- **Stars:** 10,940 ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** BSD-2-Clause
+- **Last Commit:** Mar 30, 2026
+- **Category:** voice-ai, phone-agents
+- **Best for:** real-time AI phone agents for reservations and order taking
+
+---
+
+#### [Bolna](https://github.com/bolna-ai/bolna)
+> **Description:** Bolna describes itself as an end-to-end open source voice agent orchestration platform for building LLM-driven conversational applications. The README highlights orchestration across ASR, LLM, and TTS providers over websockets, plus a production-minded structure for voice-first assistants. That makes it useful for restaurants that want AI reception, call routing, order capture, or after-hours phone support while retaining control of the deployment. The repository is smaller than Pipecat but focused directly on voice agent flows. Last commit: Nov 18, 2025. Stars: 553. Primary language: Python. License: MIT.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/bolna-ai/bolna](https://github.com/bolna-ai/bolna)
+- **Stars:** 553 ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** Nov 18, 2025
+- **Category:** voice-ai, call-automation
+- **Best for:** building self-hosted inbound and outbound restaurant call flows
+
+---
+
+#### [Intervo](https://github.com/Intervo/Intervo)
+> **Description:** Intervo positions itself as an open source conversational AI platform for advanced, goal-oriented voice and chat agents. Its README emphasizes multimodal agents, a node-based workflow canvas, RAG knowledge bases, Twilio integration, speech provider flexibility, and a web widget. For restaurants, those features are directly useful for reservations, customer service, lead capture for catering, or phone triage before a human picks up. The project also exposes how to self-host the full stack, which matters when a restaurant group wants control over data and integrations. Last commit: Jul 11, 2025. Stars: 320. Primary language: JavaScript. License: MIT.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/Intervo/Intervo](https://github.com/Intervo/Intervo)
