+# Contributing
+
+Thanks for contributing to `awesome-best-ai-tools-for-restaurants-2026`.
+
+## Submission Rules
+
+- Every submission must include a public `github.com` repository URL.
+- No proprietary SaaS products, closed-source vendors, or homepage-only tools.
+- The repository must be relevant to restaurants through a clear use case such as reservations, voice ordering, menu OCR, demand forecasting, recommendation, staff copilots, or restaurant operations.
+- Include these fields in your pull request:
+  - Tool name
+  - GitHub URL
+  - Short description based on the repository README
+  - Stars
+  - Primary language
+  - License
+  - Latest visible GitHub activity date
+  - Best restaurant use case
+- If a tool is no longer maintained, note that explicitly.
+- If a category is thin, do not force weak additions. Document the gap instead.
+
+## Pull Request Checklist
+
+- Confirm the repo is public and accessible.
+- Confirm the repo still exists on GitHub.
+- Confirm the license is visible on GitHub.
+- Confirm the description is specific and factual.
+- Keep formatting consistent with existing entries.
+
+## Quality Standard
+
+This repository is intentionally strict. We prefer fewer high-signal entries over padded lists. If a tool does not clearly belong, open an issue first instead of adding it directly.
