+# Best AI Tools for Restaurants in 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-restaurants-2026?style=social)
+
+> Best AI tools for restaurants in 2026 are still a niche in open source, so this list focuses on the strongest self-hosted GitHub projects restaurants can actually adapt for phone ordering, menu OCR, staff copilots, demand forecasting, and reservations. Every entry below is a public GitHub repository, and categories with thin restaurant-specific coverage are called out honestly as gaps.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `tastyigniter/TastyIgniter` is the strongest restaurant-specific open source platform in this list for online ordering, reservations, and restaurant operations.
+- `pipecat-ai/pipecat`, `Intervo/Intervo`, and `RasaHQ/rasa` are the most practical foundations for AI phone ordering, reservations, and support agents.
+- `PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR`, `JaidedAI/EasyOCR`, and `tesseract-ocr/tesseract` are the best menu digitization and document OCR picks.
+- `langgenius/dify`, `FlowiseAI/Flowise`, `Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm`, and `open-webui/open-webui` are the easiest ways to ship self-hosted restaurant copilots and knowledge bots.
+- `Nixtla/neuralforecast`, `unit8co/darts`, and `sktime/pytorch-forecasting` are the strongest open source forecasting stacks for demand, staffing, and inventory planning.
+
+## Why This List
+Restaurants need AI tools they can audit, self-host, and integrate with their own menus, POS data, reservation workflows, and support channels. The best AI tools for restaurants in 2026 are not mostly restaurant-only products on GitHub; the real open source opportunity is combining restaurant software with general-purpose voice AI, OCR, RAG, and forecasting projects that restaurants can run without proprietary SaaS lock-in.
+
+## Open Source Tools
