+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for restaurants in 2026?
+If you need restaurant-specific operations first, start with `TastyIgniter`. If you need AI phone agents, start with `Pipecat`, `Intervo`, or `Rasa`. If you need menu OCR, start with `PaddleOCR` or `EasyOCR`. If you need an internal restaurant copilot, start with `Dify`, `AnythingLLM`, `Onyx`, or `Open WebUI`.
+
+### Are there many restaurant-specific AI repositories on GitHub?
+No. That is the main gap this list surfaced. Most strong GitHub options are general-purpose open source AI tools that can be adapted for restaurant workflows, while restaurant-native repositories remain sparse.
+
+### Which self-hosted AI tools are best for restaurant phone ordering and reservations?
+`Pipecat`, `Bolna`, `Intervo`, and `Rasa` are the strongest picks here. Choose `Rasa` if you need strict business rules and channel integrations, `Pipecat` if you need real-time voice orchestration, and `Intervo` if a visual workflow builder matters.
+
+### Which GitHub repos are best for digitizing restaurant menus and invoices?
+`PaddleOCR`, `Tesseract`, `EasyOCR`, `OCRmyPDF`, `docTR`, and `Unstructured` are the best fit. `OCRmyPDF` is especially useful when the source is scanned PDFs, while `PaddleOCR` is stronger when you need richer parsing output.
+
+### What is the best open source restaurant knowledge base or staff copilot?
+For fast deployment, `AnythingLLM` and `Open WebUI` are the easiest. For more workflow logic, use `Dify` or `Flowise`. For larger multi-location document search, `Onyx`, `Haystack`, and `RAGFlow` are stronger foundations.
+
+### Which open source forecasting libraries are good for restaurant demand planning?
+`NeuralForecast`, `Darts`, `sktime`, and `PyTorch Forecasting` are the best options in this list. Use them for daypart sales forecasting, labor scheduling, prep forecasting, and anomaly detection across stores.
+
